  "openQuestions": [
    "Optional texts: the brief lists optional eyebrow-caps and gatch-20 elements and heading sizes h2-caps and sackers-40. They come from rooms-individual/14 ('A Landmark Reimagined') and dining-zuma/10 ('other dining options', a Gatch paragraph and venue labels), but none is visible in either crop; they look like layers hidden behind the full-bleed image or bleeding in from the section above. Cautious call: not built, all 24 instances are identical. If they should show, add an optional header row above the columns in a later entry.",
    "Book now link: no booking engine URL in the snapshot. Plan uses href '#'; the build session or Stephen supplies the real URL (likely the Marriott booking link, opening in a new tab).",
    "Newsletter form: no provider is named. Plan uses a native Webflow form (name 'newsletter', one required email field) with Webflow's default success and error copy. Confirm the provider (Webflow forms or an email platform embed) and the copy.",
    "Bonvoy logo asset is not uploaded (webflowAssetId null). Upload figma/brand/bonvoy.svg first. Unknown whether the logo should link to Marriott Bonvoy.",
    "No mobile frame exists in the snapshot (only 1600 desktop frames). Tablet and mobile styles are proposals: the columns stack below 768px and the vertical divider becomes a short horizontal rule.",
    "Shared names is-chamfer, is-wide and text-style-caption are proposals; K01 should reconcile them with the button and caption names other wave 2 plans propose.",
    "Image placement: the background image and logo need a manual Designer step under KTD10 unless the build session proves MCP placement works."
  ],
  "deviations": [
    "No container-large inside padding-global: the two columns are centred on the quarter lines of the full 1600 frame (x 400 and 1200). A 80rem container would pull them inward to about 480 and 1120.",
    "Button typography (CAPS-CAPTION-16) sits on the is-chamfer combo instead of a separate text-style-caps-caption-16 class, because a button carrying four stacked classes is fragile in Webflow.",
    "Heading tags are h2 with heading-style-h1 styling: Morello 60/72 maps to heading-style-h1 in figma/tokens.json, but every page already has its own h1."
  ]
